{{Quote|Allows the user to turn into a leopard, granting enhanced agility and powerful melee attacks.|Shop}}
'''Leopard''' was a {{Mythical}} [[Beast]]-type [[Blox Fruit]] that used to cost {{Money|5,000,000}} or {{Robux|3,000}} from the [[Blox Fruit Dealer]].

Leopard allowed the user to acquire powerful and violent attacks, as well as to transform into an anthropomorphic {{w|leopard}}, granting them speed, agility and offense. This fruit was easily abusable due to it having no Fury Meter and low cooldown moves that could be spammed, which allowed the user to rapidly cast out attacks to easily kill another player in PvP. 

Leopard was the third-most expensive fruit and was widely considered to be a decent choice for [[PvP mechanics|PvP]]. It was the first fruit to have a Robux value that exceeded the [[Fruit Notifier]]. This fruit had a strong demand in trading due to its PvP potential, cost, and rarity, often referred to as the "King of Spam" by players, due to its low cooldowns and fast moves. 

Despite having an M1 and [[Area of Effect|AoE]] attacks, Leopard was considered decent to mediocre for grinding. The M1 hitboxes were often inconsistent and hard to hit. Moreover, the attacks were generally frustrating to use due to their high knockback and lack of stuns. However, this fruit remained a good choice for [[Sea Events]], [[Raids]], and fighting tough [[Bosses]].

