==Trivia==
* During Leopard's '''[V] Transformation''', the user gained a moderate speed boost/buff. Using [[Rabbit V3]] and the [[Pilot Helmet]] added up even more speed buffs. Combining all of them made the user surpass the speed of Awakened [[Light|Light's]] '''[F] Shining Flight''', which is the second fastest flight move in the game.
* When transformed, the user was 'immune' to all environment [[lava]] puddles, such as those found in [[Raids]] or on the island [[Hot and Cold]] (This was because the hitbox when transforming is above the lava, preventing the user from taking damage). The user, however, could be harmed by the lava puddles by being dragged down by an ability such as [[Flame|Flame's]] {{Ability|Flame|V}} move.
* After the usage of {{Ability|Leopard|C}}, the user gained a temporary but strong speed boost/buff and giving them slightly faster M1's while being lit on fire. Keep in mind that this effect will not change any other attribute/aspect of the user. (Damage, Defense, Health, etc.)
** This move could also be added onto the transformation combination to make it even faster.
* [[Mammoth]], [[Buddha]], [[Yeti]], [[Phoenix]], and Leopard [[Transformation|transformations]] did not have a time limit or [[Fury Meter]] unlike fruits such as [[Dragon]], [[Venom]], [[T-Rex]], [[Gas]] or [[Kitsune]] without getting damaged, which means the user could stay transformed for as long as they like.
** The exception is [[Phoenix]]'s transformation, since it depends from amount of energy and HP the player has.
* Jumping into {{Ability|X}}while it is moving caused it to carry the player forward for a short distance. Do note that this most often worked on devices with poor connections.
* When transforming, a faint leopard ghost appeared above the user with red glowing eyes for a few milliseconds. If the player was entering the server for the first time, the leopard model sometimes appeared T-posing.
* Leopard's [M1] attacks could damage [[Sea Beast]]s.
* Leopard was widely considered a ''spammable'' fruit. Using the combination of [[Zebra Cap]] (or [[Oni Helmet]]), [[Ghoul]] V3/V4, which has the ability to reduce cooldowns, would massively contribute to the fruit's ''spammability'', so much that if used properly, the player could almost use the moves continuously.
* While transformed, the player kept their hair/hat.
* [[Yeti]] and Leopard were the third pair of fruits to share the same price, the second being [[Gas]] and [[Control]], and the first being [[Mammoth]] and [[T-Rex]].
* [[Yeti]] was considered the rival of this fruit, until it 'evolved' to [[Tiger]] to challenge it.
* {{Ability|Z}}and {{Ability|X}}could fling fruits on the ground.
* There used to be a glitch where using {{Ability|X}} would reset the players [[Air Jump]] count.
* There also used to be a glitch with {{Ability|X}} where, if lined up correctly with another player, it could kick players out of a [[Safe Zone]] despite them not being [[PvP mechanics|in combat]].
* This is the only removed Fruit to appear in a update banner ([[Updates/17.3|Update 17.3]]).

